Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Mon Jun 22 14:19:55 2026 -0700

    Bug 2047364 - Remove nsIPop3URL XPCOM interface. r=mkmelin


    The nsIPop3URL interface carried request state (pop3Sink, messageUri) on
    what should have been a plain URL. This prevented the URL from being
    serializable across processes and went against necko's assumption that
    nsIURI implementations are just URLs.

    Changes:
    - Delete nsIPop3URL.idl. The nsPop3URL class is eliminated entirely;
      pop3:// URIs now use the base nsMsgMailNewsUrl component directly
      via @mozilla.org/messenger/msgmailnewsurl;1.
    - Inline DEFAULT_POP3_PORT / DEFAULT_POP3S_PORT into
      Pop3ProtocolInfo.getDefaultServerPort().
    - nsMailboxService::CreatePop3URI (the former nsPop3URL::NewURI) now
      encodes the message key and folder URI as query parameters
      (?number=...&folderURI=...) in the pop3:// URL.
    - Pop3Channel.sys.mjs now creates its own nsIPop3Sink instead of
      QI-ing the URI. It reads uidl, number, and folderURI from the
      query string and configures the sink directly.
    - nsLocalMailFolder::OnStartRunningUrl no longer QIs to nsIPop3URL;
      the sink setup is handled by Pop3Channel before calling it.
      OnStopRunningUrl uses SchemeIs("pop"/"pop3") instead of QI.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306599

